      "block_id": "2605.28615_p14_b8",
      "text": "Image Describing Details. Before we prompt the VLM to do the describing tasks, we restrict the image to\nfollow the following rules: 1) with dimension \"color\", \"shape\", or \"texture\", the image should contain one or\ntwo objects 2) with dimension \"spatial\" or \"non-spatial\", the image should contain exactly two objects. 3)\nno repeated classes in the image; each object must belong to a unique class. We use specific prompts for\ndifferent dimensions. Examples of \u201ccolor\u201d and \u201cspatial\u201d dimension are shown in Listing 3 and Listing 4. The\nprompts for \u201cshape\u201d, \u201ctexture\u201d, and \u201cnon-spatial\u201d dimensions are similar to the \u201ccolor\u201d and \u201cspatial\u201d ones,\nrespectively. We use Qwen2.5-VL-72B-Instruct [2] as our VLM to describe the images.\n",
